@div proverb 21.d2

D.21.d2.2. gala-e {ŋiš}ma₂-gur še gur nu#-[...]
#lem: gala[lamentation singer]; magur[barge]; še[barley]; gur[unit of capacity]; X
#tr.en: @note{= Alster 1997 21 Sec. D 2} A lamentation singer …… not …… a @fsux{gur} weight of barley …… barge ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.21.d2.2

@end proverb

@div proverb 21.d3

D.21.d3.3. gala-e a-šag₄ lu₂-u₃-ka še zuh-zuh-de₃ i₃-ŋen
#lem: gala[lamentation singer]; ašag[field]; lu[person]; še[barley]; zuh[steal]; ŋen[go]
#tr.en: @note{= Alster 1997 21 Sec. D 3} A lamentation priest went into a man's field to steal the barley. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.21.d3.3

#etcsl#eq = Alster 1997 21 Sec. D 3

D.21.d3.4. lugal a-šag₄-ga-ke₄ ba-an-dab₅
#lem: lugal[king]; ašag[field]; dab[seize]
#tr.en: The owner of the field caught him. @q{“My beautiful head got confused! 
#etcsl: line-id=D.21.d3.4

D.21.d3.5. saŋ an-sag₉-ga-ŋu₁₀ bi₂-suh bi₂-bir-bir# X
#lem: saŋ[head]; sag[good]; suh[extract]; bir[scatter]; X
#tr.en: It is totally bewildered. Just let me straighten it out, 
#etcsl: line-id=D.21.d3.5

D.21.d3.6. si ga-ba-ab-sa₂ umuš-ŋu₁₀ ga-ba-da-ab-X [...]
#lem: si[horn]; sa[equal]; umuš[consideration]; X; X
#tr.en: let me …… my senses! 
#etcsl: line-id=D.21.d3.6

D.21.d3.7. ga-ba-ŋen-e-[še]
#lem: ŋen[go]
#tr.en: Let me go free!”} 
#etcsl: line-id=D.21.d3.7

@end proverb

